summary:
FAIL. I raised five new findings: four High and mandatory violations, and one Low.

- F-DG6-120 (REQ-S16-029): the env SecretProvider resolves any server environment variable, and there is no egress host allow-list. An ADM_TECH can therefore make the API send OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET (or DATABASE_URL) as a Bearer header to any https host through the connector test. I reproduced this end to end. `resolvable` is also an oracle for which variables exist. The assistant, SMTP and S3 settings share the same surface, by source reading.
- F-DG6-121 (REQ-S10-002): GET /transformations/{id}/audit applies no sensitivity rule. A TL who gets 404 on a sensitive benefit reads its events and the measured amount.
- F-DG6-122 (REQ-S10-002): /audit-events redacts only the parent's own events. A sensitive benefit's measurement events, with their amounts, reach a non-admitted AUD.
- F-DG6-123 (REQ-S10-002): the form-record versions, comments and attachments of a sensitive benefit answer 200 to a TL who gets 404 on the record, and the TL can still post comments on it.
- F-DG6-124 (Low, REQ-S02-006): the route-inventory sweep skips a table that does not exist, 'user_session', instead of 'session', so it fails spuriously under load. It has no product effect.

The candidate is confirmed: 7d6b4a9f, 2708 files, source 3cce3d4, checked in full and sparse clones. Every required check ran:
- build, typecheck (serial run, after two OOM kills), lint, format (re-runs, after my own repro file interfered), openapi (932 operations) and no-cdn all exit 0;
- historical DG5, DG4, DG3, DG2 and DG1 PASS in the repository tree;
- pnpm test on Node 22 (v22.22.0, not 22.22.2) and Node 24: full clean runs exit 0 with 2817, 2018 and 259 tests;
- integration C.UTF-8: 410/410 files, 4144 tests;
- integration with LANG unset: 409/410 files, the only failure being F-DG6-124's test defect.

Every non-zero exit is explained in its check: load timeouts, OOM kills, a vitest fork lost under load, the sparse-copy ENOENT, my repro file, background time limits, and one void unbuilt-copy run.
